{{!--
    The arrival sting's Announced tier — a brass chevron plate that drops
    from the top of the screen, sits for a few seconds, and slides back.

    Markup is V1's .bi-banner verbatim (design/ui/console.js's buildBanner),
    reused rather than reinvented — only the lane that hosts it, and the data
    that fills it, are new. scripts/foundry/sting.mjs owns the timers; this
    is purely presentational.

    capWord and role are computed by the caller from `kind`, so this template
    never has to know the mapping — it only prints what it is handed.

    The kind modifier is four separate {{#if}} blocks rather than a
    concatenated `bi-banner--{{kind}}`, matching every other dynamic class in
    this module's templates (frame.hbs's `bi-frame--concealed`, deck-cast's
    `is-selected`). tier0-architecture.test.mjs's class lint can
    only see a literal class name that sits OUTSIDE a {{ }} expression — a
    concatenated one disappears into the stripped text, and the lint could
    never have caught the eighteen-skills-in-one-column bug that way either.
--}}
<div class="bi-banner{{#if isInfo}} bi-banner--info{{/if}}{{#if isCaution}} bi-banner--caution{{/if}}{{#if isAlert}} bi-banner--alert{{/if}}{{#if isResonance}} bi-banner--resonance{{/if}}" role="{{role}}">
    <div class="bi-banner__face">
        <span class="bi-banner__cap"><span class="bi-banner__kind">{{capWord}}</span></span>
        <span class="bi-banner__chev" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
        <span class="bi-banner__glass">
            <span class="bi-banner__text">{{text}}</span>
            <span class="bi-banner__count"{{#unless showCount}} hidden{{/unless}}>&times;{{count}}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="bi-banner__cap bi-banner__cap--right"><span class="bi-banner__time">{{time}}</span></span>
    </div>
</div>
